From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pyroshine Vendor Maintenance <vendor@pyroshine.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:46:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] encoder: signal the 4:2:0 chroma sample position

A converter decides where its 4:2:0 chroma samples sit: a 2x2 box filter
centers them, while decoders that receive no position assume left siting
(the H.264/H.265 default, and FFmpeg/libplacebo for AV1), reconstructing
chroma half a luma pixel away. Add ColorDescription::chroma_location and
write it as chroma_loc_info in H.264/H.265 VUI and as AV1
chroma_sample_position, for 4:2:0 only. AV1 cannot express centered
siting; producers must generate left or co-located samples for it.
---
 src/encoder/av1/session_params.rs  |  9 +++-
 src/encoder/h264/session_params.rs | 10 ++++-
 src/encoder/h265/session_params.rs | 11 +++--
 src/encoder/mod.rs                 | 67 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/lib.rs                         |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

